      "message": "fix(setup-align): accept 2D Chamfer in a setup that holds the part turned\n\n2D Chamfer reads the same doors as 2D Contour: the picked region\nthrough OpFrame::pose_in_setup, the machine area from the setup-frame\nsection, and the top plane through the shared height law. A proof test\nnow pins it, so the kind joins setup_align::verified_kind and the list\nin the refusal message.\n\nsetup_align_chamfer cuts a chamfer with CM-0600-90 on one picked edge,\nclosed to its face loop by extend_to_loop_in, on an L prism turned\n90 degrees about X and Z. The turned setup and the baked part cut the\nsame moves, verify clean, simulate with no gouge and post the same\nprogram. The ride rings the turned top face (X 10..20, Y -5..5, Z 15).\nThe part as modelled cuts a different path.\n\nThe older tests that used 2D Chamfer as the refused example use Deburr\n(#2284) now.\n\nFixes #2283\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
